%SIXMD 1
# @?DSH - DAIMOS NATIVE SHELL

## @?OPTIONS

### @?-L - RUN AS A LOGIN SHELL
READ /CONFIG/DSH.PROFILE AND THEN HOME/.DSH.PROFILE BEFORE THE INTERACTIVE LOOP.
MISSING PROFILES ARE IGNORED.  A PROFILE ERROR IS DIAGNOSED AND LEAVES A
NONZERO STATUS WITHOUT ABORTING THE LOGIN SHELL.  WITHOUT -L, DSH DOES NOT
READ EITHER PROFILE IMPLICITLY.

### @?-C STRING - EXECUTE ONE COMMAND RECORD
EXECUTE STRING AND PASS FOLLOWING OPERANDS AS POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS.

## @?OPERANDS

### @?[SCRIPT]
S6REC SHELL SCRIPT TO EXECUTE.  FOLLOWING OPERANDS BECOME POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS.

## DESCRIPTION

DSH IS THE NATIVE WORD-STREAM DAIMOS SHELL.  IT EXECUTES BUILTINS FIRST AND
SEARCHES EXTERNAL COMMANDS IN /SYSTEM/EXEC AND /OPTION/BASE/EXEC.  EXECUTABLE
ARGUMENTS AND ENVIRONMENT RECORDS USE THE CURRENT COUNTED SIXBIT RUN V2 ABI.

INPUT IS UPPERCASED AT THE INTERACTIVE TERMINAL.  # STARTS A COMMENT OUTSIDE
QUOTES ONLY WHERE A NEW TOKEN MAY BEGIN; INSIDE A WORD IT IS ORDINARY DATA.
SINGLE QUOTES ARE FULLY LITERAL.  DOUBLE QUOTES PRESERVE ONE WORD AND LITERAL
WILDCARDS WHILE STILL ALLOWING VARIABLE EXPANSION.  EMPTY SINGLE OR DOUBLE
QUOTES CREATE A REAL EMPTY ARGUMENT.  OUTSIDE QUOTES BACKSLASH QUOTES THE NEXT
CHARACTER; INSIDE DOUBLE QUOTES IT QUOTES ONLY ", \\, OR $.

VARIABLE EXPANSION SUPPORTS $NAME, $?, $#, $$, AND $@@.  EXPORTED VARIABLES
ARE PASSED TO CHILDREN.  COMMAND SUBSTITUTION $(...) REMAINS RESERVED AND
RETURNS STATUS 126; IT WAS ALSO RESERVED IN DAIMOSV1.

LISTS USE ;.  AND EXECUTES ITS RIGHT SIDE AFTER SUCCESS; OR AFTER FAILURE;
NOT INVERTS STATUS.  ! CONNECTS A NATIVE WORD PIPE.  & STARTS A BACKGROUND
JOB.  <, >, AND >> PROVIDE INPUT, OUTPUT, AND APPEND REDIRECTION.
PIPELINES ARE BOUNDED TO EIGHT STAGES.

UNQUOTED * AND ? PERFORM BOUNDED PATHNAME GLOBBING AFTER VARIABLE EXPANSION.
QUOTED WILDCARDS REMAIN LITERAL.  IF A PATTERN HAS NO MATCH, DSH KEEPS THE
ORIGINAL PATTERN AS ONE ARGUMENT.

COMPOUND FORMS ARE:

IF LIST THEN LIST [ ELSE LIST ] FI
FOR NAME IN WORD... DO LIST DONE
WHILE LIST DO LIST DONE
UNTIL LIST DO LIST DONE
CASE WORD IN WHEN PATTERN [ PATTERN ... ] DO LIST [ WHEN PATTERN ... DO LIST ] ESAC
BEGIN LIST END
( LIST )
DEF NAME DO LIST DONE

DEF STORES A BOUNDED FUNCTION AST.  A FUNCTION RECEIVES ITS OWN POSITIONAL
ARGUMENTS AND MAY USE RETURN [STATUS].  FUNCTION COUNT, STORED NODE COUNT, AND
CALL DEPTH ARE FIXED SO SHELL MEMORY USE DOES NOT GROW AT RUN TIME.

CASE TESTS ARMS IN ORDER.  * AND ? USE THE SAME MATCHER AS PATHNAME GLOBBING;
QUOTING MAKES THEM LITERAL.  THE FIRST MATCHING ARM WINS.

## @?SUBCOMMANDS

### @?CD DIR
CHANGE THE CURRENT DIRECTORY.

### @?SET [NAME VALUE]
LIST VARIABLES OR SET NAME TO VALUE.

### @?UNSET NAME
REMOVE A SHELL VARIABLE.

### @?EXPORT NAME [VALUE]
MARK NAME FOR CHILD ENVIRONMENTS, OPTIONALLY SETTING VALUE.

### @?UMASK [MODE]
PRINT OR SET THE PROCESS FILE CREATION MASK.

### @?READ NAME
READ ONE S6REC INPUT RECORD INTO NAME.

### @?SHIFT [NUMBER]
REMOVE NUMBER POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS; THE DEFAULT IS ONE.

### @?SOURCE FILE
EXECUTE FILE IN THE CURRENT SHELL.  . FILE IS AN ALIAS.

### @?ALIAS [NAME [WORD...]]
LIST ALIASES OR DEFINE A SIMPLE COMMAND-WORD REPLACEMENT.

### @?UNALIAS NAME
REMOVE AN ALIAS.

### @?JOBS
LIST BOUNDED BACKGROUND JOBS.

### @?WAIT [PID]
WAIT FOR A CHILD OR JOB.

### @?FG [JOB]
CONTINUE A JOB IN THE FOREGROUND AND GIVE IT THE CONTROLLING TERMINAL.

### @?BG [JOB]
CONTINUE A STOPPED JOB IN THE BACKGROUND.

### @?RETURN [STATUS]
RETURN FROM A FUNCTION.

### @?EXIT [STATUS]
EXIT THE SHELL.

## @?FILES

### @?/CONFIG/DSH.PROFILE
SYSTEM LOGIN-SHELL PROFILE.

### @?HOME/.DSH.PROFILE
PER-USER LOGIN-SHELL PROFILE.

### @?/SYSTEM/EXEC
PRIMARY SYSTEM COMMAND DIRECTORY.

### @?/OPTION/BASE/EXEC
SECONDARY BASE COMMAND DIRECTORY.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - LAST COMMAND SUCCEEDED
### @?1 - COMMAND REPORTED FAILURE
### @?2 - INVALID BUILTIN USAGE WHEN APPLICABLE
### @?126 - COMMAND FORM OR EXECUTABLE COULD NOT BE RUN
### @?127 - COMMAND WAS NOT FOUND

